  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 112 PM MDT Wed Aug 5 2026\n\nWildfire smoke not quite as bad but still present at least\nthrough tomorrow. Air Quality advisories remain in effect for\nseveral counties but not as pronounced in some areas.\nTemperatures in a moderating trend now with low elevations back\ninto the 90s for high temperatures on Thursday and they will\napproach 100 Friday into Sunday. Presence of smoke can always\naffect just how warm it gets under these ridges as well. For now\nno heat products have been issued but they may be necessary\nbeginning on Friday. Dewpoints are much lower than the previous\nheat events over southeast Idaho. Hot and dry conditions are\nexpected through Sunday. The extended grids show a very slight\nchance of some convective activity in the far southern mountains\nMonday through Wednesday but low confidence in any precipiation\noccurring but it does show some monsoonal moisture returning.\nBut overall through the early part of next week the general\ntheme will remain hot and dry with some smoke presence possibly \nreducing temperatures when it's present.",
